{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "content.pages",
  "name": "Pages under a parent, their grid rows, paragraphs and item fields",
  "functions": ["content.pages", "content.paragraphs", "content.grid-rows"],
  "skill": "dw-content-modelling",
  "inputs": {"section": "content.pages", "required": ["pages"]},
  "modes": {
    "mcpOnly": {"usable": true, "reason": "Every step finds, writes and reads back with MCP tools."},
    "hosted": {"usable": true, "reason": "Nothing here needs SQL or a recycle."},
    "local": {"usable": true},
    "layerDelivered": "verify"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "pages",
      "title": "Ensure each page under its parent by menu text",
      "forEach": "pages[*]",
      "key": "{item.menuText}",
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-children", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_pages_by_parent_id", "arguments": {"parentId": "{step.pages[item.parent].id|0}", "areaId": "{build.areaId}"}, "rows": "data", "match": {"menuText": "{item.menuText}"}, "compare": {"itemType": "{item.itemType}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"}
      ], "conflict": {"reason": "another page already answers at the input's path, so a new page would be served at the path with -1 and the old page would keep the address (and every link to it); point the input at that page, or remove or move the other page first", "skipWhen": {"path": "item.path", "exists": false}, "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-path-owner", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "fetch_frontend_page_html", "arguments": {"path": "{item.path}"}, "rows": "$", "match": {"statusCode": 200}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"}
      ]}},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-create", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md",
          "create": {"operation": "save_pages", "arguments": {"pages": [{"id": 0, "areaId": "{build.areaId}", "parentPageId": "{step.pages[item.parent].id|0}", "menuText": "{item.menuText}", "urlName": "{item.urlName}", "itemType": "{item.itemType}", "active": true, "sort": "{item.sort|null}"}]}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_pages_by_parent_id", "arguments": {"parentId": "{step.pages[item.parent].id|0}", "areaId": "{build.areaId}"}, "rows": "data", "match": {"menuText": "{item.menuText}"}, "expect": {"itemType": "{item.itemType}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "itemType goes on the create call; changing it later deletes the page's item and its field values. The page id is read back by parent and menu text, never carried between runs or hosts. A url name another page already holds is not refused: the new page is served at <path>-1 and the save answers success, so before a create the step reads the input's path (find.conflict) and blocks the item when another page answers there; a base sample page in a navigation folder can own a root path.",
      "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "page-title",
      "title": "Keep each page's Title equal to its menu text",
      "forEach": "pages[*]",
      "key": "{item.menuText}",
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-page-fields", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_page_item_field_values", "arguments": {"pageId": "{step.pages.id}"}, "rows": "data", "compareMap": {"from": {"Title": "{item.menuText}"}, "key": "fieldSystemName", "value": "value"}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"}
      ]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-title", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md",
          "update": {"operation": "set_page_item_fields", "arguments": {"pageId": "{step.pages.id}", "fields": {"Title": "{item.menuText}"}}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_page_item_field_values", "arguments": {"pageId": "{step.pages.id}"}, "rows": "data", "expectMap": {"from": {"Title": "{item.menuText}"}, "key": "fieldSystemName", "value": "value"}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "On an item-typed page every save re-derives the menu text from the item's title field, reorder_pages included, so a page created with an empty Title loses its menu text at its next save.",
      "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "page-slug",
      "title": "Pin the url name of each page whose Title this run wrote",
      "forEach": "pages[*]",
      "key": "{item.menuText}",
      "after": {"step": "page-title", "states": ["UPDATED"]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-slug", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md",
          "create": {"operation": "save_pages", "arguments": {"pages": [{"id": "{step.pages.id}", "urlName": "{item.urlName}"}]}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_pages_by_parent_id", "arguments": {"parentId": "{step.pages[item.parent].id|0}", "areaId": "{build.areaId}"}, "rows": "data", "match": {"id": "{step.pages.id}"}, "expect": {"menuText": "{item.menuText}"}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "A Title write on a page without a pinned url name moves its address. No page read projects urlName, so only the served path proves the slug.",
      "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "rows",
      "title": "Ensure each grid row on its page by sort, with its definition and container",
      "forEach": "pages[*].rows[*]",
      "key": "{parent.menuText}/{item.sort}",
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-rows", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_grid_rows_by_page_id", "arguments": {"pageId": "{step.pages[parent.menuText].id}"}, "rows": "data", "match": {"sort": "{item.sort}"}, "compare": {"definitionId": "{item.definitionId}", "container": "{item.container}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-swift-building/references/grid-rows-and-binding.md"}
      ]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-save-row", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-swift-building/references/grid-rows-and-binding.md",
          "create": {"operation": "save_grid_rows", "arguments": {"gridRows": [{"id": 0, "pageId": "{step.pages[parent.menuText].id}", "container": "{item.container}", "definitionId": "{item.definitionId}", "itemType": "{item.itemType}", "sort": "{item.sort}"}]}},
          "update": {"operation": "save_grid_rows", "arguments": {"gridRows": [{"id": "{found.id}", "container": "{item.container}", "definitionId": "{item.definitionId}"}]}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_grid_rows_by_page_id", "arguments": {"pageId": "{step.pages[parent.menuText].id}"}, "rows": "data", "match": {"sort": "{item.sort}"}, "expect": {"definitionId": "{item.definitionId}", "container": "{item.container}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-swift-building/references/grid-rows-and-binding.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "container is load-bearing: a row under a container the layout does not render is stored, reads back, and puts nothing on the page while it answers HTTP 200. Take it from get_layout_containers and the definition from get_row_definitions.",
      "source": "skills/dw-swift-page-design/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "paragraphs",
      "title": "Ensure each paragraph in its row by sort, with its item type and column",
      "forEach": "pages[*].paragraphs[*]",
      "key": "{parent.menuText}/{item.row}/{item.sort}",
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-paragraphs", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_paragraphs_by_page_id", "arguments": {"pageId": "{step.pages[parent.menuText].id}"}, "rows": "data", "match": {"gridRowId": "{step.rows[parent.menuText,item.row].id}", "sort": "{item.sort}"}, "compare": {"itemType": "{item.itemType}", "gridRowColumn": "{item.column}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-swift-page-design/SKILL.md"}
      ]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-save-paragraph", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-swift-page-design/SKILL.md",
          "create": {"operation": "save_paragraphs", "arguments": {"paragraphs": [{"id": 0, "pageId": "{step.pages[parent.menuText].id}", "itemType": "{item.itemType}", "template": "{item.template|null}", "gridRowId": "{step.rows[parent.menuText,item.row].id}", "gridRowColumn": "{item.column}", "sort": "{item.sort}"}]}},
          "update": {"operation": "save_paragraphs", "arguments": {"paragraphs": [{"id": "{found.id}", "gridRowColumn": "{item.column}"}]}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_paragraphs_by_page_id", "arguments": {"pageId": "{step.pages[parent.menuText].id}"}, "rows": "data", "match": {"gridRowId": "{step.rows[parent.menuText,item.row].id}", "sort": "{item.sort}"}, "expect": {"itemType": "{item.itemType}", "gridRowColumn": "{item.column}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-swift-page-design/SKILL.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "A cell renders exactly one paragraph. Changing itemType on an existing paragraph deletes its item and field values, so the update never sends it.",
      "source": "skills/dw-swift-page-design/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "paragraph-fields",
      "title": "Write each paragraph's item fields, a button field as its full JSON or empty",
      "forEach": "pages[*].paragraphs[*]",
      "key": "{parent.menuText}/{item.row}/{item.sort}",
      "skipWhen": {"path": "item.fields", "exists": false},
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-field-values", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_paragraph_item_field_values", "arguments": {"paragraphId": "{step.paragraphs.id}"}, "rows": "data", "compareMap": {"from": "{item.fields}", "key": "fieldSystemName", "value": "value"}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"}
      ]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-set-fields", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-extend-mcp-tools/references/backend-mcp-server.md",
          "update": {"operation": "set_paragraph_item_fields", "arguments": {"paragraphId": "{step.paragraphs.id}", "fields": "{item.fields}"}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_paragraph_item_field_values", "arguments": {"paragraphId": "{step.paragraphs.id}"}, "rows": "data", "expectMap": {"from": "{item.fields}", "key": "fieldSystemName", "value": "value"}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "set_paragraph_item_fields counts the fields it was asked to write, not the ones it matched; the read-back names a misspelt field. A bare create stores the item type's string defaults in button fields, which render a ConverterException inside an HTTP 200 page: give every button field its full ButtonData JSON with a Label or Link, or an empty string for no button; the tool refuses a ButtonData JSON with neither.",
      "source": "skills/dw-swift-page-design/SKILL.md"
    }
  ],
  "debts": [],
  "verify": {
    "checkIds": ["content.pages.exist", "content.paragraphs.visible", "content.paragraphs.item-instances", "content.grid-rows.rows", "content.grid-rows.container-set", "content.grid-rows.paragraph-placement"],
    "probes": [
      {
        "id": "page-unique",
        "title": "Each page exists exactly once under its parent",
        "forEach": "pages[*]",
        "minimumSubjects": 1,
        "bindings": [
          {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_pages_by_parent_id", "arguments": {"parentId": "{step.pages[item.parent].id|0}", "areaId": "{build.areaId}"}, "rows": "data", "match": {"menuText": "{item.menuText}"}, "assert": {"kind": "count", "op": "eq", "value": 1}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"}
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "row-container",
        "title": "Each grid row carries the container the input names",
        "forEach": "pages[*].rows[*]",
        "minimumSubjects": 1,
        "bindings": [
          {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_grid_rows_by_page_id", "arguments": {"pageId": "{step.pages[parent.menuText].id}"}, "rows": "data", "match": {"sort": "{item.sort}"}, "assert": {"kind": "equals", "path": "container", "value": "{item.container}"}, "source": "skills/dw-swift-building/references/grid-rows-and-binding.md"}
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "page-renders",
        "title": "A public page answers 200 at its path with its Title",
        "forEach": "pages[*]",
        "skipWhen": {"path": "item.path", "exists": false},
        "minimumSubjects": 1,
        "pollSeconds": 20,
        "bindings": [
          {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "fetch_frontend_page_html", "arguments": {"path": "{item.path}"}, "rows": "$", "match": {"statusCode": 200}, "assert": {"kind": "contains", "path": "title", "value": "{item.menuText}"}, "source": "skills/dw-swift-page-design/SKILL.md"}
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "page-path",
        "title": "Each page is served at the input's path, not at a path the platform suffixed (-1) because another page holds it (a server whose fetch follows the redirect reports finalPath; an older one answers 301 and names the target)",
        "forEach": "pages[*]",
        "skipWhen": {"path": "item.path", "exists": false},
        "minimumSubjects": 1,
        "pollSeconds": 20,
        "bindings": [
          {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "fetch_frontend_page_html", "requiresSchema": {"output": ["finalPath"]}, "arguments": {"path": "/Default.aspx?ID={step.pages[item.menuText].id}"}, "rows": "$", "match": {"statusCode": 200}, "assert": {"kind": "equals", "path": "finalPath", "value": "{item.path}"}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"},
          {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "fetch_frontend_page_html", "arguments": {"path": "/Default.aspx?ID={step.pages[item.menuText].id}"}, "rows": "$", "match": {"statusCode": 301}, "assert": {"kind": "equals", "path": "error", "value": "Page redirects to: {item.path}"}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"}
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "page-render-clean",
        "title": "Each page renders without an error the stored fields cannot show (an error dump, a missing image or icon file, text in its own background colour)",
        "forEach": "pages[*]",
        "minimumSubjects": 1,
        "bindings": [
          {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "inspect_page_render", "arguments": {"pageId": "{step.pages[item.menuText].id}"}, "rows": "issues", "match": {"severity": "error"}, "assert": {"kind": "count", "op": "eq", "value": 0}, "source": "skills/dw-content-modelling/references/page-paragraph-writes.md"}
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "provenOn": [
    {"dwVersion": "10.30.6", "mcpVersion": "0.6.3-BETA", "date": "2026-11-19", "evidence": "content.pages.1-verify.json (all WOULD-CREATE), content.pages.2-apply.json (12 of 12), content.pages.3-verify.json and content.pages.4-apply-again.json (10 of 10, nothing changed), content.pages.6-mcponly-apply.json (12 of 12 from empty, MCP only), content.pages.10-final-verify.json and content.pages.11-final-verify-mcponly.json (10 of 10); the pages answered HTTP 200 with the written copy and no ConverterException"},
    {"dwVersion": "10.30.6", "mcpVersion": "0.6.6-BETA", "date": "2026-11-19", "evidence": "the whole-build recipe set on a fresh fictional input after the add-in was rolled 0.6.3-BETA -> 0.6.6-BETA (Update-HostAddIn): 1-verify (all eleven recipes WOULD-CREATE), 2-apply, 3-verify (11 of 11 recipes), 4-apply-again (nothing written, no debt owed), 5-verify after a brand restore (11 of 11); the same input then verified 11 of 11 on the add-in rolled back to 0.6.3. 6-mcponly is an MCP-only apply on a second fresh input. This recipe: 9 of 9 with the new page-render-clean probe (inspect_page_render reports no error-severity issue); MCP-only 9 of 9."}
  ],
  "traps": [
    "Never carry a page id between runs or hosts: ids are minted per host and a deserialize re-mints them. Pages are found by parent and menu text at the point of use.",
    "Read the item type, row definition, container and template names from get_item_types, get_row_definitions, get_layout_containers and get_paragraph_templates (areaId always passed).",
    "On a multi-language website every save on the master creates the mirror with the structure and not the field values; write on the master, then set the mirror's values.",
    "A URL answers 404 for several seconds after a correct save; poll it to 200 before reading a 404 as a failure.",
    "fetch_frontend_page_html returns a summary (statusCode, title, h1Tags, counts), not the markup: it proves the page answers, not that a paragraph rendered without an error block."
  ]
}
